REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANGKA REGENCY

NUMBER 9 OF 2019

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF BANGKA,

Considering:

a. that women's empowerment is carried out so that women can actualize their potential optimally to participate in development in accordance with their nature and capacity;
b. that women as national assets who play a role in the process of continuation and preparation of quality generations, need to receive guarantees of their rights and protection from acts of violence and discrimination in order to build society, nation and state;
c. that based on the provisions of Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, mandates that women's empowerment is a mandatory affair implemented by the Regency Regional Government;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Protection;

In View of:

1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 28 of 1959 concerning Stipulation of Emergency Law Number 4 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1956 Number 55) Emergency Law Number 5 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1956 Number 56) and Emergency Law Number 6 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1956 Number 57) concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions including Kotaparaja Within the Level I Region of South Sumatra as Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1959 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1821);
3. Law Number 27 of 2000 concerning the Establishment of Bangka Belitung Islands Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 217, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 4033);
4. Law Number 1 of 1974 concerning Marriage (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1945 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1974 Number 1, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3019);
5. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
6. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165 Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
7. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);
8. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
9. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635), as amended by Law Number 31 of 2014 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5601);
10. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
11. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4967);
12. Law Number 36 of 2009 concerning Health (State Gazette Year 2009 Number 144, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5063);
13. Law Number 19 of 2011 concerning Ratification of the Convention On The Rights Of Persons with Disabilities (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 107, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5251);
14. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5589) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
15. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
16. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 67 of 2011 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions;
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 1 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Improving the Quality of Life of Women;
18. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Women's Protection;
19. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 4 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Empowerment of Community Institutions in the Field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BANGKA REGENCY

and

REGENT OF BANGKA

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION.

text:
Pasal 2

Ruang lingkup Peraturan Daerah ini meliputi:
a. Hak perempuan;
b. kewajiban dan tanggungjawab Pemerintah Daerah Kabupaten;
c. pemberdayaan perempuan;
d. perlindungan perempuan;
e. strategi pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan;
f. pelaksanaan perlindungan perempuan;
g. mekanisme penyelenggaraan pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan;
h. pembiayaan; dan
i. pembinaan dan pengawasan.

translated_text:
Article 2

The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. women's rights;
b. obligations and responsibilities of the Regency Regional Government;
c. women's empowerment;
d. women's protection;
e. women's empowerment and protection strategy;
f. implementation of women's protection;
g. mechanism for organizing women's empowerment and protection;
h. financing; and
i. guidance and supervision.

text:
Pasal 3

Pemberdayaan dan Perlindungan Perempuan dilaksanakan berdasarkan asas:
a. penghormatan terhadap hak asasi manusia;
b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
c. non diskriminasi; dan
d. kepentingan terbaik perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 3

Women's Empowerment and Protection is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect for human rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination; and
d. the best interests of women.

text:
BAB II

HAK PEREMPUAN

Pasal 5

1. Setiap perempuan berhak untuk:
a. hidup dan mempertahankan hidup serta meningkatkan taraf kehidupannya;
b. memenuhi kebutuhan dasarnya untuk tumbuh dan berkembang secara layak, berkeluarga dan melanjutkan keturunan;
c. mengembangkan pribadinya, untuk memperoleh pendidikan, dan  meningkatkan kualitas hidupnya agar menjadi manusia yang beriman,  bertaqwa, bertanggungjawab, berakhlak mulia, bahagia, dan sejahtera  sesuai dengan hak asasi manusia;
d. memperoleh keadilan, rasa aman, dan kebebasan menyampaikan pendapat tanpa diskriminasi;
e. terlibat dalam setiap tahapan proses pembangunan;
f. bebas dari perbudakan/diperhambat dan ancaman;
g. memperoleh perlindungan diri pribadi, keluarga, kehormatan, martabat dan hak miliknya;
h. mendapatkan kesejahteraan dan kehidupan yang layak;
i. berpartisipasi dalam politik;
j. melakukan perbuatan hukum; dan
k. bebas memilih pasangan dalam perkawinannya.
2. Setiap perempuan selama dalam ikatan perkawinan mempunyai hak dan tanggung jawab yang sama dengan suaminya atas semua hal yang  berkenaan dengan kehidupan perkawinannya, hubungan dengan  anak-anaknya, dan kepemilikan serta pengelolaan harta bersama sesuai dengan peraturan perundang-undangan.
3. Setelah putusnya perkawinan, seorang perempuan mempunyai hak dan  tanggung jawab dengan mantan suaminya atas semua hal yang berkenaan  dengan anak dengan memperhatikan kepentingan terbaik bagi anak.

translated_text:
CHAPTER II

WOMEN'S RIGHTS

Article 5

1. Every woman has the right to:
a. live and maintain life and improve her standard of living;
b. fulfill her basic needs to grow and develop properly, have a family and continue offspring;
c. develop her personality, to obtain education, and improve her quality of life to become a faithful, pious, responsible, noble, happy, and prosperous human being in accordance with human rights;
d. obtain justice, security, and freedom to express opinions without discrimination;
e. be involved in every stage of the development process;
f. be free from slavery/servitude and threats;
g. obtain protection of her person, family, honor, dignity and property rights;
h. obtain welfare and a decent life;
i. participate in politics;
j. perform legal acts; and
k. freely choose a partner in her marriage.
2. Every woman during marriage has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband over all matters relating to her married life, relationship with her children, and ownership and management of joint property in accordance with statutory regulations.
3. After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has rights and responsibilities with her former husband over all matters relating to children with due regard to the best interests of the child.

text:
Pasal 8

Pemberdayaan perempuan dibidang ekonomi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 7 huruf a dilaksanakan melalui:
a. pemberian keterampilan dan pelatihan kerja;
b. fasilitasi pembentukan kelompok usaha ekonomi produktif;
c. fasilitasi penguatan dan pengembangan kelompok usaha ekonomi produktif;
d. fasilitasi dan bantuan permodalan; dan
e. fasilitasi pengembangan jaringan pemasaran.

translated_text:
Article 8

Empowerment of women in the economic field as referred to in Article 7 letter a shall be implemented through:
a. provision of skills and job training;
b. facilitation of the formation of productive economic business groups;
c. facilitation of strengthening and development of productive economic business groups;
d. facilitation and capital assistance; and
e. facilitation of marketing network development.

text:
Pasal 9

Pemberdayaan perempuan di bidang sosial budaya sebagaimana dimaksud  dalam Pasal 7 huruf b dilaksanakan melalui:
a. peningkatan pengetahuan, sikap dan keterampilan untuk mendorong pemenuhan pendidikan secara berjenjang sesuai dengan potensi untuk meningkatkan status sosial;
b. peningkatan kesadaran, kemauan dan kemampuan untuk mengatasi;
c. permasalahan kesehatan melalui upaya promotif, preventif, kuratif, dan  rehabilitative yang berkualitas utamanya dibidang kesehatan reproduksi;
d. peningkatan kesadaran dan pengetahuan tentang perencanaan keluarga;
e. mandiri, sehat dan sejahtera termasuk akses layanan konsultasi dan  pencatatan perkawinan; dan
f. fasilitasi dan upaya pelestarian adat istiadat dan pengembangan ilmu  pengetahuan, teknologi, seni dan budaya untuk kemajuan perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 9

Empowerment of women in the socio-cultural field as referred to in Article 7 letter b shall be implemented through:
a. improvement of knowledge, attitudes and skills to encourage the fulfillment of tiered education in accordance with potential to improve social status;
b. improvement of awareness, willingness and ability to overcome;
c. health problems through quality promotive, preventive, curative, and rehabilitative efforts, especially in the field of reproductive health;
d. improvement of awareness and knowledge about family planning;
e. independent, healthy and prosperous including access to consultation services and marriage registration; and
f. facilitation and efforts to preserve customs and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women.

text:
Pasal 13

Pelaksanaan perlindungan perempuan diberikan kepada:
a. perempuan pekerja/buruh;
b. perempuan lanjut usia;
c. perempuan penyandang disabilitas;
d. perempuan tunawisma;
e. perempuan pekerja rumah tangga;
f. perempuan kepala keluarga;
g. perempuan mantan warga binaan lembaga pemasyarakatan;
h. perempuan korban bencana;
i. perempuan pekerja seks komersial; dan
j. perempuan korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 13

Implementation of protection of women shall be provided to:
a. women workers/laborers;
b. elderly women;
c. women with disabilities;
d. homeless women;
e. domestic women workers;
f. women heads of household;
g. women former inmates of correctional institutions;
h. women disaster victims;
i. commercial sex women workers; and
j. women victims of violence.

text:
Pasal 14

1. Pelaksanaan perlindungan bagi perempuan pekerja/buruh sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 13 huruf a untuk memberikan perlindungan dari  tindakan eksploitasi ekonomi dan perlakuan kejam, tidak manusiawi dan  mengusahakan penghargaan yang layak atas pekerjaannya.
2. Perempuan pekerja/buruh sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1)  mendapatkan perlindungan atas:
a. pengakuan hak, upah dan kondisi kerja yang layak;
b. jaminan kesehatan dan sosial;
c. akses informasi dan layanan konsultasi hukum;
d. kesempatan memperoleh pengetahuan dan keterampilan untuk meningkatkan status; dan
e. saksi dan korban.

translated_text:
Article 14

1. Implementation of protection for women workers/laborers as referred to in Article 13 letter a is to provide protection from acts of economic exploitation and cruel, inhumane treatment and to seek proper appreciation for their work.
2. Women workers/laborers as referred to in paragraph (1) shall receive protection for:
a. recognition of rights, wages and decent working conditions;
b. health and social security;
c. access to information and legal consultation services;
d. opportunities to obtain knowledge and skills to improve status; and
e. witnesses and victims.

text:
Pasal 17

1. Pelaksanaan perlindungan bagi perempuan tunawisma sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 13 huruf d dalam rangka memberikan perlindungan  dan pencegahan terhadap bentuk-bentuk kekerasan yang disebabkan oleh  tidak adanya tempat berlindung atau tempat tinggal tetap.
2. Perempuan tunawisma sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) mendapat hak perlindungan atas:
a. tempat tinggal yang layak;
b. jaminan kesehatan dan sosial;
c. pencatatan administrasi kependudukan;
d. kesempatan memperoleh keterampilan untuk meningkatkan status  ekonomi; dan
e. akses informasi dan layanan konsultasi hukum.

translated_text:
Article 17

1. Implementation of protection for homeless women as referred to in Article 13 letter d is in order to provide protection and prevention against forms of violence caused by the absence of shelter or permanent residence.
2. Homeless women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall receive protection rights for:
a. decent housing;
b. health and social security;
c. population administration registration;
d. opportunities to obtain skills to improve economic status; and
e. access to information and legal consultation services.

text:
BAB X

PEMBINAAN DAN PENGAWASAN

Pasal 28

1. Bupati melakukan pembinaan dan pengawasan penyelenggaraan  pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan.
2. Bentuk pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) adalah sebagai  berikut:
a. memberikan sosialisasi kepada masyarakat dan dunia usaha mengenai;
b. kebijakan pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan;
c. menyediakan buku, leaflet, brosur mengenai pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan, dan isu-isu terkait lainnya serta  menyebarluaskannya kemasyarakat;
d. fasilitasi peningkatan kapasitas lembaga penyelenggara pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan;
e. fasilitasi forum partisipasi perempuan dan organisasi perempuan;
f. fasilitasi layanan rehabilitasi dan reintegrasi perempuan korban bencana dan korban kekerasan;
g. mengoordinasikan peran serta dunia usaha dan kelembagaan lain, termasuk bantuan internasional bagi pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan; dan
h. memberikan penghargaan kepada masyarakat dan dunia usaha baik  secara individu maupun kelembagaan yang telah melakukan upaya  pemberdayaan dan perlindungan perempuan.
3. Bentuk pengawasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat berupa  kegiatan monitoring dan evaluasi atas pemberdayaan dan perlindungan  perempuan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER X

GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 28

1. The Regent conducts guidance and supervision of the organization of women's empowerment and protection.
2. Forms of guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) are as follows:
a. providing socialization to the community and business world regarding;
b. women's empowerment and protection policies;
c. providing books, leaflets, brochures regarding women's empowerment and protection, and other related issues and disseminating them to the community;
d. facilitating capacity building of institutions organizing women's empowerment and protection;
e. facilitating forums for women's participation and women's organizations;
f. facilitating rehabilitation and reintegration services for women victims of disaster and victims of violence;
g. coordinating the participation of the business world and other institutions, including international assistance for women's empowerment and protection; and
h. providing awards to the community and business world both individually and institutionally who have made efforts to empower and protect women.
3. Forms of supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of monitoring and evaluation activities on women's empowerment and protection.
